module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistSection.NonvanishingEq
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Variety.Projective.RationalPointHyperplane

/-!
# The hyperplane of a rational point of an arbitrary graded `Proj`

Let `𝒜` be a nonnegatively graded ring generated in degree one over its degree-zero part, let
`k` be a field mapping to `𝒜 0` by a ring homomorphism `γ`, and give the degree-one part `𝒜 1`
the `k`-module structure `γ` determines. A point `q` of `Proj 𝒜` that is hit by a section of
the structure morphism `Proj 𝒜 ⟶ Spec k` — a `k`-rational point — has a **hyperplane**: the
degree-one elements vanishing at `q` are the kernel of a nonzero `k`-linear functional on
`𝒜 1`, and that hyperplane cuts out `q` alone. Over an infinite field a single degree-one
element therefore vanishes at `q` and at none of finitely many other given points.

This is the content of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Variety/Projective/RationalPointHyperplane.lean` freed from the
symmetric algebra: there the graded ring is `Sym_k V` and the hyperplane is produced from the
`Sym`-specific description of the point cut out by a functional, which is unavailable for a
general graded ring. The replacement is
`Stacks.GradedRationalPoint.toIdeal_eq_degreeOneIdeal`, and it is the only genuinely new
argument here.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.GradedRationalPoint.toSpecBase`: the morphism `Proj 𝒜 ⟶ Spec k` built from
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.toSpecZero` and a ring homomorphism `γ : k →+* 𝒜 0`. Keeping `γ`
  arbitrary is what lets a consumer feed in a structure morphism it has by some other route,
  rather than having to identify its degree-zero part with `k` on the nose.
* `Stacks.GradedRationalPoint.pointSubmodule`: the degree-one elements vanishing at a point.
* `Stacks.GradedRationalPoint.awayFraction`: the degree-zero fraction `v / f` of two degree-one
  elements.
* `Stacks.GradedRationalPoint.degreeOneIdeal`: the ideal generated by the degree-one elements
  vanishing at a point.

## Main results

* `Stacks.GradedRationalPoint.exists_dual_pointSubmodule_eq_ker`: **the hyperplane of a rational
  point.** The degree-one elements vanishing at `q` are the kernel of a `k`-linear functional
  taking the value `1` at any chosen degree-one element outside `q`.
* `Stacks.GradedRationalPoint.exists_add_mem_adjoin`: the degree-one equations of `q` together
  with one chart variable span the whole ring; this is where degree-one generation enters.
* `Stacks.GradedRationalPoint.toIdeal_eq_degreeOneIdeal`: **a point whose degree-one equations
  contain those of a rational point is that point**, both homogeneous primes being the ideal
  generated by the degree-one equations of the rational point.
* `Stacks.GradedRationalPoint.exists_mem_degreeOne_forall_notMem`: **one degree-one element
  vanishing at a rational point and at none of finitely many other points**, over an infinite
  field.

## Implementation notes

The `k`-module structure on `𝒜 1` is a hypothesis together with its compatibility `hγ` with
`γ`, rather than being built here from `γ`: `Module ↥(𝒜 0) ↥(𝒜 1)` is not an instance, so a
structure derived from `γ` could not be found by instance search at the use sites anyway, and a
consumer that already has a `k`-module structure on its degree-one part would have to transport
along it.

Rationality of `q` is phrased as "a morphism `Spec k ⟶ Proj 𝒜` over the base whose image is
`q`", not as `AlgebraicGeometry.IsRationalPoint`. That is exactly the data the argument uses —
`AlgebraicGeometry.ptOfIsRationalPoint` is how the `IsRationalPoint` form produces it — and it
is also the form in which a rational point of a scheme immersed in `Proj 𝒜` hands one over,
with no residue-field comparison in between.

That the degree-zero part is a field is used only through `hfield`, and only to see that a
homogeneous prime meets `𝒜 0` in zero.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B58](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B58)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01M7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01M7)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory HomogeneousLocalization

universe u w

namespace Stacks.GradedRationalPoint

variable {A : Type u} {σ : Type u} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜]

/-! ### The degree-one part as a vector space over a base field -/

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] [Module k ↥(𝒜 1)] (γ : k →+* ↥(𝒜 0))

/-- The canonical morphism of a graded `Proj` to the spectrum of a base field, through a ring
homomorphism from the field to the degree-zero part. -/
def toSpecBase : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜 ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.toSpecZero 𝒜 ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom γ)

variable {𝒜}

/-- The space of degree-one elements vanishing at a point of `Proj 𝒜`. -/
def pointSubmodule (hγ : ∀ (c : k) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)), ((c • v : ↥(𝒜 1)) : A) = (γ c : A) * (v : A))
    (q : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) : Submodule k ↥(𝒜 1) where
  carrier := {v | (v : A) ∈ q.asHomogeneousIdeal}
  zero_mem' := by
    simp
  add_mem' {a b} ha hb := by
    simpa using q.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.add_mem ha hb
  smul_mem' c v hv := by
    simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq, hγ c v]
    exact q.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal.mul_mem_left _ hv

/-- A degree-one element lies in `pointSubmodule γ hγ q` if and only if it lies in the homogeneous
prime ideal of `q`. -/
theorem mem_pointSubmodule_iff
    (hγ : ∀ (c : k) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)), ((c • v : ↥(𝒜 1)) : A) = (γ c : A) * (v : A))
    (q : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)) :
    v ∈ pointSubmodule γ hγ q ↔ (v : A) ∈ q.asHomogeneousIdeal := Iff.rfl

/-! ### The degree-zero fractions attached to degree-one elements -/

/-- The degree-zero fraction `v / f` in the homogeneous localization away from a degree-one
element `f`. -/
def awayFraction {f : A} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)) : Away 𝒜 f :=
  Away.mk 𝒜 hf 1 (v : A) (by simp)

/-- The underlying element of `awayFraction hf v` in the localization is the fraction `v / f`. -/
theorem val_awayFraction {f : A} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)) :
    (awayFraction hf v).val =
      Localization.mk (v : A) ⟨f ^ 1, (Submonoid.mem_powers_iff _ _).mpr ⟨1, rfl⟩⟩ :=
  rfl

/-- The image of a degree-zero element `c` in a homogeneous localization has underlying element
`c / 1`. -/
theorem val_fromZeroRingHom (x : Submonoid A) (c : ↥(𝒜 0)) :
    (fromZeroRingHom 𝒜 x c).val = Localization.mk (c : A) 1 :=
  rfl

/-- The fraction `(v + w) / f` is the sum of `v / f` and `w / f`. -/
@[simp]
theorem awayFraction_add {f : A} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) (v w : ↥(𝒜 1)) :
    awayFraction hf (v + w) = awayFraction hf v + awayFraction hf w := by
  apply val_injective
  rw [val_add, val_awayFraction, val_awayFraction, val_awayFraction, Localization.add_mk_self]
  rfl

/-- The fraction `f / f` is `1`. -/
theorem awayFraction_self {f : A} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1) :
    awayFraction hf ⟨f, hf⟩ = 1 := by
  apply val_injective
  rw [val_one, val_awayFraction]
  simp only [pow_one]
  exact Localization.mk_self_mk _ _

/-- The fraction `(c • v) / f` is the product of the image of `γ c` and `v / f`. -/
theorem awayFraction_smul {f : A} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 1)
    (hγ : ∀ (c : k) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)), ((c • v : ↥(𝒜 1)) : A) = (γ c : A) * (v : A))
    (c : k) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)) :
    awayFraction hf (c • v) =
      fromZeroRingHom 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f) (γ c) * awayFraction hf v := by
  apply val_injective
  rw [val_mul, val_awayFraction, val_awayFraction, val_fromZeroRingHom, Localization.mk_mul,
    one_mul, hγ c v]

/-! ### The functional cut out by a rational point -/

omit [Module k ↥(𝒜 1)] in
/-- On the chart `D₊(v₀)`, a point read as a ring map `ψ` to `k` kills the fraction `v / v₀`
exactly when `v` lies in the homogeneous prime of the point. -/
private theorem apply_awayFraction_eq_zero_iff {v₀ : A} (hv₀ : v₀ ∈ 𝒜 1)
    (ψ : CommRingCat.of (Away 𝒜 v₀) ⟶ CommRingCat.of k) (cp : Spec (CommRingCat.of k))
    {q : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜}
    (hq : (Spec.map ψ ≫ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι 𝒜 v₀ hv₀ Nat.one_pos).base cp = q)
    (v : ↥(𝒜 1)) :
    ψ.hom (awayFraction hv₀ v) = 0 ↔ (v : A) ∈ q.asHomogeneousIdeal := by
  have hiso : Away.isLocalizationElem (𝒜 := 𝒜) (d := 1) (e := 1) hv₀ v.2 =
      awayFraction hv₀ v := by
    apply val_injective
    rw [val_awayFraction]
    show Localization.mk _ _ = Localization.mk _ _
    simp only [pow_one]
  have hpre : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι 𝒜 v₀ hv₀ Nat.one_pos ⁻¹ᵁ
        AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (v : A) =
      PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen (awayFraction hv₀ v) := by
    rw [← hiso]
    exact AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι_preimage_basicOpen (𝒜 := 𝒜) (f := v₀) (g := (v : A))
      (f_deg := hv₀) (hm := Nat.one_pos) (g_deg := v.2) (hm' := Nat.one_pos)
  have h1 : q ∈ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (v : A) ↔
      (Spec.map ψ).base cp ∈ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι 𝒜 v₀ hv₀ Nat.one_pos ⁻¹ᵁ
          AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (v : A) :=
    Iff.of_eq (congrArg (fun y : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜 =>
      y ∈ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (v : A)) hq.symm)
  have h2 : awayFraction hv₀ v ∈ ((Spec.map ψ).base cp).asIdeal ↔
      ψ.hom (awayFraction hv₀ v) = 0 := by
    show awayFraction hv₀ v ∈ Ideal.comap ψ.hom cp.asIdeal ↔ _
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, (Ideal.eq_bot_or_top cp.asIdeal).resolve_right cp.isPrime.ne_top,
      Ideal.mem_bot]
  have h4 : (v : A) ∉ q.asHomogeneousIdeal ↔ ψ.hom (awayFraction hv₀ v) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [← AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.mem_basicOpen, h1, hpre]
    exact (PrimeSpectrum.mem_basicOpen _ _).trans (not_congr h2)
  exact (not_iff_not.mp h4).symm

/-- **The hyperplane of a rational point.** If a point `q` of `Proj 𝒜` is hit by a section of
the structure morphism to `Spec k`, then the degree-one elements vanishing at `q` are the kernel
of a `k`-linear functional on `𝒜 1` taking the value `1` at any chosen degree-one element
outside `q`. -/
theorem exists_dual_pointSubmodule_eq_ker
    (hγ : ∀ (c : k) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)), ((c • v : ↥(𝒜 1)) : A) = (γ c : A) * (v : A))
    (q : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) (τ : Spec (CommRingCat.of k) ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜)
    (hsec : τ ≫ toSpecBase 𝒜 γ = 𝟙 _) (hpt : ∀ a, τ.base a = q)
    {v₀ : A} (hv₀ : v₀ ∈ 𝒜 1) (hv₀q : v₀ ∉ q.asHomogeneousIdeal) :
    ∃ φ : Module.Dual k ↥(𝒜 1),
      φ ⟨v₀, hv₀⟩ = 1 ∧ pointSubmodule γ hγ q = LinearMap.ker φ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨cp⟩ : Nonempty (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) := ⟨IsLocalRing.closedPoint k⟩
  -- the affine chart `D₊(v₀)` around the point
  have hrange : Set.range τ.base ⊆
      Set.range (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι 𝒜 v₀ hv₀ Nat.one_pos).base := by
    rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩
    rw [hpt a]
    have hmem : q ∈ (↑(AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι 𝒜 v₀ hv₀ Nat.one_pos).opensRange :
        Set (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜)) := by
      rw [AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.opensRange_awayι]
      exact hv₀q
    exact hmem
  -- the rational point, read on that chart as a `k`-algebra map `ψ` to `k`
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψ⟩ : ∃ ψ : CommRingCat.of (Away 𝒜 v₀) ⟶ CommRingCat.of k,
      Spec.map ψ ≫ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι 𝒜 v₀ hv₀ Nat.one_pos = τ :=
    ⟨Spec.preimage (IsOpenImmersion.lift _ _ hrange),
      by rw [Spec.map_preimage, IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac]⟩
  have hqψ : (Spec.map ψ ≫ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι 𝒜 v₀ hv₀ Nat.one_pos).base cp = q := by
    rw [hψ, hpt]
  -- `ψ` is a `k`-algebra map: the point lies over `Spec k`
  have hψk : ∀ c : k, ψ.hom (fromZeroRingHom 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers v₀) (γ c)) = c := by
    have hcomp : CommRingCat.ofHom (γ : k →+* ↥(𝒜 0)) ≫
        CommRingCat.ofHom (fromZeroRingHom 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers v₀)) ≫ ψ =
        𝟙 (CommRingCat.of k) := by
      apply Spec.map_injective
      rw [Spec.map_id, Spec.map_comp, Spec.map_comp,
        ← AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι_toSpecZero 𝒜 v₀ hv₀ Nat.one_pos, Category.assoc,
        Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc (Spec.map ψ), hψ]
      exact hsec
    exact fun c => congrArg (fun g : CommRingCat.of k ⟶ CommRingCat.of k => g.hom c) hcomp
  -- assemble the functional
  refine ⟨{ toFun := fun v => ψ.hom (awayFraction hv₀ v)
            map_add' := fun v w => by simp only [awayFraction_add, map_add]
            map_smul' := fun c v => by
              rw [awayFraction_smul γ hv₀ hγ c v, _root_.map_mul, hψk c]
              rfl }, ?_, ?_⟩
  · show ψ.hom (awayFraction hv₀ ⟨v₀, hv₀⟩) = 1
    rw [awayFraction_self hv₀, map_one]
  · ext v
    rw [mem_pointSubmodule_iff, LinearMap.mem_ker]
    exact (apply_awayFraction_eq_zero_iff hv₀ ψ cp hqψ v).symm

/-! ### A rational point is determined by its degree-one equations -/

variable (𝒜)

/-- The ideal generated by the degree-one elements vanishing at a point of `Proj 𝒜`. -/
def degreeOneIdeal (q : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) : Ideal A :=
  Ideal.span {a : A | a ∈ 𝒜 1 ∧ a ∈ q.asHomogeneousIdeal}

variable {𝒜}

/-- The ideal `degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q` is homogeneous. -/
theorem isHomogeneous_degreeOneIdeal (q : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) :
    Ideal.IsHomogeneous 𝒜 (degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q) :=
  Ideal.homogeneous_span 𝒜 _ fun _ hx => ⟨1, hx.1⟩

/-- The ideal `degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q` is contained in the homogeneous prime ideal of `q`. -/
theorem degreeOneIdeal_le (q : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) :
    degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q ≤ q.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal :=
  Ideal.span_le.mpr fun _ ha => ha.2

/-- **The degree-one equations of a rational point and one chart variable span the ring.** Every
element of `A` is the sum of an element of the ideal generated by the degree-one elements
vanishing at `q` and a polynomial in the chart variable `v₀`: this is where degree-one generation
of `𝒜` is used. -/
theorem exists_add_mem_adjoin
    (hγ : ∀ (c : k) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)), ((c • v : ↥(𝒜 1)) : A) = (γ c : A) * (v : A))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin ↥(𝒜 0) ((𝒜 1 : Set A)) = ⊤) (q : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜)
    {φ : Module.Dual k ↥(𝒜 1)} {v₀ : A} (hv₀ : v₀ ∈ 𝒜 1) (hφ₀ : φ ⟨v₀, hv₀⟩ = 1)
    (hker : pointSubmodule γ hγ q = LinearMap.ker φ) (a : A) :
    ∃ j ∈ degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q, ∃ p ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(𝒜 0) ({v₀} : Set A), a = j + p := by
  classical
  set C : Subalgebra ↥(𝒜 0) A :=
    { carrier := {b : A | ∃ j ∈ degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q,
        ∃ p ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(𝒜 0) ({v₀} : Set A), b = j + p}
      mul_mem' := by
        rintro x y ⟨j, hj, p, hp, rfl⟩ ⟨j', hj', p', hp', rfl⟩
        refine ⟨j * j' + (j * p' + p * j'), ?_, p * p', mul_mem hp hp', by ring⟩
        exact add_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hj)
          (add_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hj) (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hj'))
      one_mem' := ⟨0, Submodule.zero_mem _, 1, one_mem _, (zero_add _).symm⟩
      add_mem' := by
        rintro x y ⟨j, hj, p, hp, rfl⟩ ⟨j', hj', p', hp', rfl⟩
        exact ⟨j + j', add_mem hj hj', p + p', add_mem hp hp', by ring⟩
      zero_mem' := ⟨0, Submodule.zero_mem _, 0, zero_mem _, (zero_add _).symm⟩
      algebraMap_mem' := fun r =>
        ⟨0, Submodule.zero_mem _, algebraMap ↥(𝒜 0) A r, algebraMap_mem _ r, (zero_add _).symm⟩ }
  have hsub : ((𝒜 1 : Set A)) ⊆ (C : Set A) := by
    intro v hv
    refine ⟨v - (γ (φ ⟨v, hv⟩) : A) * v₀, ?_,
      (γ (φ ⟨v, hv⟩) : A) * v₀, ?_, by ring⟩
    · refine Ideal.subset_span ⟨?_, ?_⟩
      · have hm := SetLike.mul_mem_graded (γ (φ ⟨v, hv⟩)).2 hv₀
        rw [zero_add] at hm
        exact sub_mem hv hm
      · have hu : (⟨v, hv⟩ - φ ⟨v, hv⟩ • ⟨v₀, hv₀⟩ : ↥(𝒜 1)) ∈ pointSubmodule γ hγ q := by
          rw [hker, LinearMap.mem_ker, map_sub, map_smul, hφ₀, smul_eq_mul, mul_one, sub_self]
        have hcoe : ((⟨v, hv⟩ - φ ⟨v, hv⟩ • ⟨v₀, hv₀⟩ : ↥(𝒜 1)) : A) =
            v - (γ (φ ⟨v, hv⟩) : A) * v₀ := by
          rw [AddSubgroupClass.coe_sub, hγ]
        exact hcoe ▸ hu
    · exact Subalgebra.smul_mem _ (Algebra.self_mem_adjoin_singleton _ _) (γ (φ ⟨v, hv⟩))
  exact Algebra.adjoin_le hsub (by simp [hgen])

/-- The homogeneous components of a polynomial in a single degree-one element `v₀` are multiples
of the corresponding power of `v₀` by a degree-zero scalar. -/
theorem exists_decompose_adjoin_singleton {v₀ : A} (hv₀ : v₀ ∈ 𝒜 1)
    {p : A} (hp : p ∈ Algebra.adjoin ↥(𝒜 0) ({v₀} : Set A)) (m : ℕ) :
    ∃ c : ↥(𝒜 0), (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 p m : A) = (c : A) * v₀ ^ m := by
  classical
  have hspan : p ∈ Submodule.span ↥(𝒜 0) ((Submonoid.closure ({v₀} : Set A) : Set A)) := by
    rwa [← Algebra.adjoin_eq_span (R := ↥(𝒜 0)) (A := A), Subalgebra.mem_toSubmodule]
  clear hp
  induction hspan using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
      rw [← Submonoid.powers_eq_closure] at hx
      obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := hx
      have hmem : v₀ ^ n ∈ 𝒜 n := by simpa using SetLike.pow_mem_graded n hv₀
      rcases eq_or_ne n m with rfl | hne
      · exact ⟨1, by simp [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 hmem]⟩
      · exact ⟨0, by simp [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne 𝒜 hmem hne]⟩
  | zero => exact ⟨0, by simp⟩
  | add x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := ihx
      obtain ⟨c', hc'⟩ := ihy
      refine ⟨c + c', ?_⟩
      rw [DirectSum.decompose_add, DirectSum.add_apply, AddMemClass.coe_add, hc, hc',
        AddMemClass.coe_add, add_mul]
  | smul r x _ ih =>
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := ih
      refine ⟨r * c, ?_⟩
      have hal : (algebraMap ↥(𝒜 0) A) r = (r : A) := rfl
      have hrc : ((r * c : ↥(𝒜 0)) : A) = (r : A) * (c : A) := rfl
      rw [Algebra.smul_def, hal, DirectSum.coe_decompose_mul_of_left_mem_zero 𝒜 r.2, hc, hrc,
        mul_assoc]

/-- **A point of `Proj 𝒜` whose degree-one equations contain those of a rational point is that
point.** Both homogeneous primes coincide with the ideal generated by the degree-one elements
vanishing at the rational point. -/
theorem toIdeal_eq_degreeOneIdeal
    (hγ : ∀ (c : k) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)), ((c • v : ↥(𝒜 1)) : A) = (γ c : A) * (v : A))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin ↥(𝒜 0) ((𝒜 1 : Set A)) = ⊤)
    (hfield : ∀ c : ↥(𝒜 0), c ≠ 0 → IsUnit (c : A))
    (q q' : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜)
    (hle : pointSubmodule γ hγ q ≤ pointSubmodule γ hγ q')
    {φ : Module.Dual k ↥(𝒜 1)} {v₀ : A} (hv₀ : v₀ ∈ 𝒜 1) (hφ₀ : φ ⟨v₀, hv₀⟩ = 1)
    (hker : pointSubmodule γ hγ q = LinearMap.ker φ)
    (hv₀q' : v₀ ∉ q'.asHomogeneousIdeal) :
    q'.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal = degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q := by
  classical
  have hJq' : degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q ≤ q'.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal :=
    Ideal.span_le.mpr fun a ha => hle (show (⟨a, ha.1⟩ : ↥(𝒜 1)) ∈ _ from ha.2)
  have key : ∀ (m : ℕ) (b : A), b ∈ 𝒜 m → b ∈ q'.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal →
      b ∈ degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q := by
    intro m b hbm hbq'
    obtain ⟨j, hj, p, hp, hb⟩ :=
      exists_add_mem_adjoin γ hγ hgen q hv₀ hφ₀ hker b
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_decompose_adjoin_singleton hv₀ hp m
    have hdj : (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 j m : A) ∈ degreeOneIdeal 𝒜 q :=
      isHomogeneous_degreeOneIdeal q m hj
    have hsum : b = (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 j m : A) + (c : A) * v₀ ^ m := by
      rw [← DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 hbm, hb, DirectSum.decompose_add,
        DirectSum.add_apply, AddMemClass.coe_add, hc]
    have hcv : (c : A) * v₀ ^ m ∈ q'.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal := by
      rw [show (c : A) * v₀ ^ m = b - (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 j m : A) by
        linear_combination -hsum]
      exact sub_mem hbq' (hJq' hdj)
    have hc0 : c = 0 := by
      by_contra hne
      exact hv₀q' (q'.isPrime.mem_of_pow_mem m
        ((Ideal.unit_mul_mem_iff_mem _ (hfield c hne)).mp hcv))
    rwa [hsum, hc0, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero, zero_mul, add_zero]
  refine le_antisymm (fun a ha => ?_) hJq'
  rw [(isHomogeneous_degreeOneIdeal q).mem_iff]
  intro m
  exact key m _ (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 a m).2 (q'.asHomogeneousIdeal.isHomogeneous m ha)

/-! ### A degree-one equation through a rational point and through no other given point -/

/-- **One degree-one element vanishing at a rational point and at none of finitely many other
points.** Let `𝒜` be generated in degree one over its degree-zero part, let the degree-zero part
be a field acting through `γ`, let `k` be infinite, let `q` be a point of `Proj 𝒜` hit by a
section of the structure morphism to `Spec k`, and let `q₁, …, qₙ` be finitely many points
distinct from `q`. Then some degree-one element of `𝒜` lies in the homogeneous prime of `q` and
in none of the homogeneous primes of the `qⱼ`.

The hyperplane of `q` is not the union of its intersections with the other points' spaces of
degree-one equations, because `k` is infinite and each of those intersections is proper: a point
whose degree-one equations contain those of `q` is `q`. -/
theorem exists_mem_degreeOne_forall_notMem [Infinite k]
    (hγ : ∀ (c : k) (v : ↥(𝒜 1)), ((c • v : ↥(𝒜 1)) : A) = (γ c : A) * (v : A))
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin ↥(𝒜 0) ((𝒜 1 : Set A)) = ⊤)
    (hfield : ∀ c : ↥(𝒜 0), c ≠ 0 → IsUnit (c : A))
    (hcov : ∀ x : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜, ∃ g : A, g ∈ 𝒜 1 ∧ g ∉ x.asHomogeneousIdeal)
    (q : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) (τ : Spec (CommRingCat.of k) ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜)
    (hsec : τ ≫ toSpecBase 𝒜 γ = 𝟙 _) (hpt : ∀ a, τ.base a = q)
    {ι : Type w} [Finite ι] (qs : ι → AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) (hne : ∀ j, q ≠ qs j) :
    ∃ v : ↥(𝒜 1), (v : A) ∈ q.asHomogeneousIdeal ∧
      ∀ j, (v : A) ∉ (qs j).asHomogeneousIdeal := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := Submodule.exists_forall_notMem_of_forall_ne_top
    (fun j => (pointSubmodule γ hγ (qs j)).comap (pointSubmodule γ hγ q).subtype) (by
      intro j htop
      have hle : pointSubmodule γ hγ q ≤ pointSubmodule γ hγ (qs j) :=
        fun x hx => htop.ge (Submodule.mem_top (x := ⟨x, hx⟩))
      obtain ⟨v₀, hv₀, hv₀qs⟩ := hcov (qs j)
      have hv₀q : v₀ ∉ q.asHomogeneousIdeal := fun hc =>
        hv₀qs (hle (show (⟨v₀, hv₀⟩ : ↥(𝒜 1)) ∈ pointSubmodule γ hγ q from hc))
      obtain ⟨φ, hφ₀, hker⟩ :=
        exists_dual_pointSubmodule_eq_ker γ hγ q τ hsec hpt hv₀ hv₀q
      have heq := fun (q' : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) hle =>
        toIdeal_eq_degreeOneIdeal γ hγ hgen hfield q q' hle hv₀ hφ₀ hker
      exact hne j (ProjectiveSpectrum.ext (HomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal_injective
        ((heq q le_rfl hv₀q).trans (heq (qs j) hle hv₀qs).symm))))
  exact ⟨w.1, w.2, hw⟩

end Stacks.GradedRationalPoint

